<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:30:42Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Behind the UK's use of AI in asylum applications</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea094185d2392ecc05093db21207e68dc209ac868dcf9c48b7ff5a416a790b53</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:29:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T15:07:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/behind-the-uk-s-use-of-ai-in-asylum-applications--7c816cd4e664.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/behind-the-uk-s-use-of-ai-in-asylum-applications" /><summary type="html">The UK is increasingly turning to artificial intelligence to manage its immigration system, from analysing migrants’ phones to processing asylum applications. But what happens when AI gets involved in deciding how an asylum seeker's story is understood? Stella Elgersma, journalist at InfoMigrants, explains how the UK Home Office is testing AI tools to process asylum applications, including a system that generates summaries of asylum interviews. With errors, limited human oversight and concerns over transparency, could AI put asylum seekers’ lives at risk?</summary></entry><entry><title>China summit ends with little new, Europe backs Ukraine in Berlin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7bcbafc4026d7aa3585d103ee0a9c18e572c4457ff05509535383ba5d1c96c02</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T14:04:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/china-summit-ends-with-little-new-europe-backs-ukraine-in-berlin" /><summary type="html">The leaders of China, the United States and Russia met in Shenzhen for a historic first, but the summit brought little new: non-binding statements on peace and no plan to meet regularly. In Berlin, Europeans gathered to show their support for Ukraine, a pointed answer to a summit where Europe had no seat, as FRANCE 24's Kethevane Gorjestani explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine's European allies meet in Berlin in show of support</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:846c3edceaed67999ba3d790c8fface0990f79e485f995e42504dc708afc7b5e</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:30:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T10:43:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ukraine-s-european-allies-meet-in-berlin-in-show-of-support--2eee6bb2adfc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-s-european-allies-meet-in-berlin-in-show-of-support" /><summary type="html">Ukraine’s main European allies are meeting in Berlin on Thursday as a show of support for Kyiv, with US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner also attending. The gathering, which brings together the leaders of Germany, France, Britain, Poland and Italy as well as NATO chief Mark Rutte, takes place as Trump and Putin meet in China, fuelling fears in Europe that decisions on the war could be made without its input. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Germany has the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Denmark ratifies Greenland security deal after months of pressure by Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6a8a63d1d63c33b4a51fdc3f015c6db168babd362398fa37914f98fbd6c0616</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:30:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T10:08:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-denmark-ratifies-greenland-security-deal-after-months-of-pressure-by-trump--274d8e9dcbf1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-denmark-ratifies-greenland-security-deal-after-months-of-pressure-by-trump" /><summary type="html">Denmark's parliament on Thursday ratified a security deal involving Greenland and the United States. The vote comes months after the US, Denmark and Greenland ​signed the ‌agreement to end a standoff with the Trump administration over the Arctic island's future.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine's allies meet in Berlin to rally support for Kyiv after Trump-Putin-Xi talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95175e0ed9ad34ceed00901547ebfb62f5ddea8c16c607fde98c55abd58b86e4</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:30:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T02:55:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-european-leaders-to-meet-in-berlin-to-support-for-ukraine-after-trump-putin-xi-talks--3d07d30f658f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-european-leaders-to-meet-in-berlin-to-support-for-ukraine-after-trump-putin-xi-talks" /><summary type="html">Ukraine's allies meet in Berlin on Thursday to shore up support for Kyiv just hours after Russia's Vladimir Putin took part in a historic trilateral meeting with US President Donald Trump and China's Xi Jinping. The "Coalition of the Willing" summit comes as Europe is hoping to secure a seat at the table of any future peace talks.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>COP31: Vanuatu calls for UN climate summit reform, warns of backsliding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:724b81326c02dddfed36006cd14395beb6fb59dfe722e938d91a53300e96e91f</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T02:00:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-cop31-vanuatu-un-climate-summit-reform-warns-of-backsliding--3de44bf4c890.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-cop31-vanuatu-un-climate-summit-reform-warns-of-backsliding" /><summary type="html">Vanuatu's Environment Minister Ralph Regenvanu has called for changes to the UN climate summit process, accusing a small group of countries of blocking progress and warning that COP31 risks reversing previous commitments.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Crimea bridge strike: Fact-checking fake videos of damage after Ukraine's attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:33d3bd5035d05cb413a77b7a30bbc070e921a813d4308edc3af85c6b2daad053</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T21:51:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261118-crimea-bridge-strike-fact-checking-fake-videos-of-damage-after-ukraine-s-attack--caeee115f4a1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261118-crimea-bridge-strike-fact-checking-fake-videos-of-damage-after-ukraine-s-attack" /><summary type="html">Ukraine struck the Kerch Bridge linking Russia to occupied Crimea, but not all the dramatic footage circulating online is real. Multiple AI-generated videos falsely show the bridge collapsed with extensive damage. Some even used branding resembling a Ukrainian news agency to appear credible. While the bridge was indeed struck and damaged, the viral videos were fabricated using AI, as Vedika Bahl explains.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Why Ukraine keeps trying to bring down Russia's bridge to Crimea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:10d5b66693261565a5cd8d6a5365711a82f17ae2899bce7c968d8ed05e9ddaf9</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T18:17:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261118-why-ukraine-keeps-trying-to-bring-down-russia-s-bridge-to-crimea--968a1a06351e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261118-why-ukraine-keeps-trying-to-bring-down-russia-s-bridge-to-crimea" /><summary type="html">A Ukrainian drone and missile strike on Monday night brought down a stretch of the bridge linking the annexed Crimean Peninsula to Russia, potentially crippling a route long used by Moscow to move men and materiel into Crimea and the southern front. Here’s why Kyiv keeps testing its strength against an infrastructure project that has become synonymous with Russian President Vladimir Putin’s 2014 seizure of the peninsula.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>War in Ukraine: Is France in direct conflict with Russia?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6250f1eb01b9535d35d2fa530f2fcb5f018e6d84bbff6ca100ef18bad76f914a</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T16:57:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261118-war-in-ukraine-is-france-in-direct-conflict-with-russia--95e35187e67d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261118-war-in-ukraine-is-france-in-direct-conflict-with-russia" /><summary type="html">An investigation published by the French public radio channel RFI on November 17 revealed that a confidential mission by the French army known as "Volia" has been used for months to conceal the presence of French personnel in Ukraine. Russia was prompt to accuse France of direct involvement in the conflict. Is this true?</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia’s new low-cost munitions pose a fresh threat to Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e7bdcf2b19170b126b2fc9bfbb0128a58f67ca8bd43a45050fcb4d46158a106c</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T16:19:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261118-russia-new-low-cost-munitions-threat-ukraine--81011c427b6e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261118-russia-new-low-cost-munitions-threat-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Dan-T, Filin and Geran-5 might not mean anything to you, but in Ukraine, everyone is talking about these munitions. These new Russian weapons are small, fast and cheap – and a major threat, as they were specially designed to get around Ukrainian anti-aircraft defences and strike deep within the country.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU proposes new €45 billion Ukraine loan to be repaid by Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e8ddb77f5fc1fdfc486bbfc5cd540eca45894654d72529fb735fd97e59ced46</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T10:42:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261118-eu-proposes-new-_45-billion-ukraine-loan-to-be-repaid-by-russia--b080f0b0d8d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261118-eu-proposes-new-%E2%82%AC45-billion-ukraine-loan-to-be-repaid-by-russia" /><summary type="html">European Commission President Ursula von ⁠der Leyen announced on Wednesday a proposed €45 billion loan to Ukraine for 2027 to help cover around two-thirds ​of Kyiv's financing ​needs. The loan will be repaid ⁠through future ⁠war reparations by Russia, von der Leyen added.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Italy approves anti-semitism law despite concerns over freedom of expression</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:27dcf091534518df90294a5e7fb3b62551e2d13acfa99edfa11de2fa40e6b78f</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T07:37:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261118-italy-approves-anti-semitism-law-despite-concerns-over-freedom-of-expression--ddabda07c6bb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261118-italy-approves-anti-semitism-law-despite-concerns-over-freedom-of-expression" /><summary type="html">Italy's ​parliament on Tuesday approved a new bill aimed at combating anti-semitism – which lists some forms of criticism of ⁠Israel as examples of anti-semitic conduct – despite concerns that it could limit freedom of expression and advocacy for Palestinian rights. The law will not impose financial ⁠penalties or criminal sanctions for offenders.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Authorities take over Turkey's last pro-opposition broadcaster Sozcu TV</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01c0f75cc1644d8436d030398138166070efbdd7290754c677ab226577005b90</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T19:58:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/authorities-take-over-turkey-s-last-pro-opposition-broadcaster-sozcu-tv--b9a43ba1ff5e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/authorities-take-over-turkey-s-last-pro-opposition-broadcaster-sozcu-tv" /><summary type="html">Police raided the Istanbul headquarters of Sozcu TV on Tuesday, dealing another significant blow to Turkey's pro-opposition media. This is the third such seizure of pro-opposition media in just over a year. It comes amid public uproar over a multi-billion investment fund scandal that has affected the savings of nearly half a million people and piled pressure on President Recep Tayyip Erdogan's ruling AKP party ahead of elections in 2028. FRANCE 24's Jasper Mortimer reports from Ankara.</summary></entry><entry><title>Estonia closes its border with Russia but can it keep Moscow out?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4f473efbffd903ff6632c442b4b3a6a2405c36458af85e3ac3308d86723114c</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T15:28:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261117-estonia-closes-its-border-with-russia-but-can-it-keep-moscow-out--8ad536e1b952.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261117-estonia-closes-its-border-with-russia-but-can-it-keep-moscow-out" /><summary type="html">Estonia announced this weekend it would close its border with Russia, after blaming its eastern neighbour of attempting to sabotage one of its drone factories. But at a time when the internet has become one of Russia’s most potent weapons to wage hybrid warfare, does closing the border even matter?</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Two bridges in Kyiv heavily damaged by Russian strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ee64e607ce65f4a92b3b7000b1f9aedcfe4a1d14f7adabfbf93520546f8b758</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T12:54:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261117-ukraine-two-bridges-in-kyiv-heavily-damaged-by-russian-strikes--7ea1ef9e1575.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261117-ukraine-two-bridges-in-kyiv-heavily-damaged-by-russian-strikes" /><summary type="html">Russia hit two major bridges in Kyiv while Ukraine struck Moscow's link to annexed Crimea for the second night in a row, officials said Tuesday, ahead of a historic meeting of Chinese, US and Russian leaders. Detals from the ground by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Kyiv, Gulliver Cragg.</summary></entry><entry><title>Data leak exposes Deutsche Bank ties to Russian oligarchs, Epstein and Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a276c0ec40fb724bf386f7c60ddc753c0df1d840e60259c3790895806199c5b1</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T09:45:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/live-news/20261117-deutsche-bank-shares-drop-after-reports-on-mass-data-leak--3c18ba74004c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20261117-deutsche-bank-shares-drop-after-reports-on-mass-data-leak" /><summary type="html">Shares in Deutsche Bank plunged Tuesday after international media outlets published reports detailing the bank's questionable business practices over the past 20 years, including its ties to Russian oligarchs, convicted sex offender Jeffrey Epstein and Donald Trump before he became the US president.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine critically damages bridge linking occupied Crimea with Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4b648ee99011a83eda51ffc5df9a9f8836bb84e7e4266b7b172d199d538b926</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T06:43:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261117-ukraine-critically-damages-bridge-linking-occupied-crimea-with-russia--6db84b4abe2c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261117-ukraine-critically-damages-bridge-linking-occupied-crimea-with-russia" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian drones and missiles struck a vital bridge linking Russia to the occupied Crimean Peninsula, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said Tuesday, calling it an “unprecedented” operation as Russia reported that its forces downed a record number of Ukrainian drones for the second straight day.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Putin arrives in China ahead of trilateral Trump-Xi summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:77e6fa1b62e786ba7c9d5d8a03e8226f00f4ea92c26ce7c198026551ae48dedb</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T01:38:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261117-live-russian-attacks-target-bridges-in-kyiv-knocking-out-heating-and-water-ukraine--ed14a50b56b5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261117-live-russian-attacks-target-bridges-in-kyiv-knocking-out-heating-and-water-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Russian President Vladimir Putin on Wednesday arrived in China where he is expected to meet with his US and Chinese counterparts Donald Trump and Xi Jinping on the sidelines of the APEC summit, Russian state media reported. Russian state news agency TASS said that Putin's plane has landed at Shenzhen's Bao'an International Airport. Putin will take part in the summit later this week. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russian strikes hit two key bridges in Kyiv, disrupting water and power supplies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:985ebb6075eec7851a9a48da4927a94e9892d3c57a627c7b2fed34ad99752c2d</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T00:58:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261117-russian-strikes-hit-two-key-bridges-in-kyiv-disrupting-water-and-power-supplies-ukraine--88719774137a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261117-russian-strikes-hit-two-key-bridges-in-kyiv-disrupting-water-and-power-supplies-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Russian forces struck two major bridges crossing the Dnipro River in Kyiv late Monday, damaging critical infrastructure and causing water and power cuts in parts of the Ukrainian capital, Mayor Vitali Klitschko said. The attacks came as Moscow launched a wider wave of drone and missile strikes across Ukraine, including in the regions of Cherkasy and Kharkiv.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Europe hunts for Palantir alternatives as militaries seek to limit US dependence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:555e577b43786f8689cc3fa8033b7615924d45e6c8b19f65a67c0df7569bb5e0</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T22:07:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261116-europe-hunts-for-palantir-alternatives-as-militaries-seek-to-limit-us-dependence--d261bbeac259.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261116-europe-hunts-for-palantir-alternatives-as-militaries-seek-to-limit-us-dependence" /><summary type="html">As Europe's ​defence ministries look to limit dependency on American technology and major software company Palantir Technologies for critical military functions, a growing number of firms within the region are competing for their business. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Arthur Holland Michel, a journalist and researcher specialising in emerging military technologies.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Europe hunts for Palantir alternatives as militaries seek to limit US dependence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d89013418bf1ee4a9300af0059be137e92147859ae6a960fbfc686f1a005999</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T22:05:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe-hunts-for-palantir-alternatives-as-militaries-seek-to-limit-us-dependence--784c998c6cef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe-hunts-for-palantir-alternatives-as-militaries-seek-to-limit-us-dependence" /><summary type="html">As Europe's ​defence ministries look to limit dependency on American technology and major software company Palantir Technologies for critical military functions, a growing number of firms within the region are competing for their business. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Arthur Holland Michel, a journalist and researcher specialising in emerging military technologies.</summary></entry><entry><title>Hard bargain: Should Ukraine trade Donbas for NATO membership?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbd5ad8c81acaea0918544bcb23a5f95482bc76d283acf9faed8f95d93d22c03</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T20:27:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261116-should-ukraine-trade-donbas-for-nato-membership--a0b9c11071ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261116-should-ukraine-trade-donbas-for-nato-membership" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky is asserting that the United States has asked him about a straight-up swap: Russia gets the Donbas and the rest of Ukraine gets NATO membership – a guarantee against Moscow later having a second go and annexing the entire country. Whether or not the offer is real, serious or either side would accept it is another matter. We ask if the talk of partition signals some kind of turning point in a nearly five-year war that's at a brutal stalemate.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>EU nations unveil Rwanda deal for migrant return hub</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1650539552fb948b3eb5f6184da024144de176feb5fe3470afb1e19d0405e664</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T20:01:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/eu-nations-unveil-rwanda-deal-for-migrant-return-hub--38d2912ee018.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/eu-nations-unveil-rwanda-deal-for-migrant-return-hub" /><summary type="html">Five EU countries including Germany and Denmark on Monday unveiled a deal to establish a migrant deportation centre in Rwanda -- the first such facility outside the bloc. The group, also comprising Austria, Greece and the Netherlands, has been gunning to open a "return-hub" despite rights groups' concerns, after the European Union cleared the way with a recent toughening of migration rules. FRANCE 24's Dave Keating reports from Brussels.</summary></entry><entry><title>Czech mass protests: Media is the first casualty 'when you want to attack democracy'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2bd889d104bdbc18cb3d8941530d6921ce5f1d9a5a1c6a9bbcca2d019ac9e77d</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T18:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/czech-mass-protests-media-is-the-first-casualty-when-you-want-to-attack-democracy--d702c00cffa6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/czech-mass-protests-media-is-the-first-casualty-when-you-want-to-attack-democracy" /><summary type="html">As hundreds of thousands of people gather in Prague to protest the Czech government's proposal to replace public broadcasting licence fees with direct state funding, Delano D'Souza is pleased to welcome Bára Stárek, Executive Director of Díky, že můžem. Stárek warns that the proposed changes offer "no real safeguards" against political influence, pointing to developments in Slovakia and Hungary. She also drew a parallel with the Velvet Revolution of 1989, recalling that "we didn't have a free media and we only had a state media" under communist rule. "Media is the first (line of) attack when you want to attack democracy," she said. With the legislation expected to reach Parliament in January, Stárek believes the demonstrations will continue if the government refuses to engage in any discussions.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia's war on Ukraine: 'Americans want to have a deal whatever the cost for both Ukraine &amp; Europe'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:49913253fd620d6d51dc71eec735be7563f3216a9c4a529025377d2625639e11</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T16:22:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-s-war-on-ukraine-americans-want-to-have-a-deal-whatever-the-cost-for-both-ukraine-europe--19378cdc5fe6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-s-war-on-ukraine-americans-want-to-have-a-deal-whatever-the-cost-for-both-ukraine-europe" /><summary type="html">Delano D'Souza is pleased to welcome Grégoire Roos, Director of the Europe and Russia and Eurasia Programmes at Chatham House. As European countries prepare to take part in the next round of Ukraine peace talks, Roos questions whether having five European representatives could weaken their negotiating position. "The other option is to realize that it dilutes the negotiating power of Europe. And I would lean towards that," he says, proposing Finnish President Alexander Stubb as a possible representative. Roos also points to differences between Washington and European governments over negotiations with Russia. While "the Americans do absolutely want to have a deal whatever the cost for both Ukraine and Europe," he argues that European governments have little choice but to maintain pressure on Moscow, which has yet to abandon its "maximalist demands."</summary></entry><entry><title>New talks held between Kyiv, Europe and the US, Zelensky says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a523d049557a555b830143c84e7044979557e73303a4524e59adcf2cb0b039d9</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T06:52:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261116-live-600-ukrainian-drones-target-moscow-strike-crimea-bridge-halts-traffic--59995b76c236.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261116-live-600-ukrainian-drones-target-moscow-strike-crimea-bridge-halts-traffic" /><summary type="html">European negotiators joined Ukrainian and US envoys online for the first time to strategise ending the Ukraine war, Ukrainian President Zelensky said Monday. This came after US President Donald Trump announced a plan to discuss the conflict during trilateral nuclear talks with Russia and China on the sidelines of the APEC summit in Shenzhen, China on Thursday. Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Hundreds of thousands of Czechs protest in Prague over public media funding plan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b1cdefb7ec5da85987a8af33c6fe2d9536abd31327364394e5d8e211b5cf44a2</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T02:28:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261116-czechs-protest-prague-public-media-funding-plan--ea96c7d8c96e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261116-czechs-protest-prague-public-media-funding-plan" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of thousands of Czechs rallied in Prague on Sunday against government plans to replace public media fees with direct state funding, which critics say threatens broadcasters’ independence. Organisers said turnout exceeded a March protest of more than 200,000, potentially making it the largest demonstration since the 1989 Velvet Revolution.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Nearly 2,200 migrants reach Spain's Canary Islands in two days</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c212ff4a93eefa46fae3679bad426bf00a05206c6a0e84bdeaf646648baad4b</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T21:06:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261115-nearly-2200-migrants-reach-spain-canary-islands-in-two-days--5944f32f14b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261115-nearly-2200-migrants-reach-spain-canary-islands-in-two-days" /><summary type="html">Nearly 2,200 migrants have reached the Canary Islands over the past two days, Spain’s coastguard said Sunday, continuing a recent surge of arrivals from West African countries to the Spanish archipelago, where the authorities declared a migration emergency earlier this week.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Prague's fight for public TV: Why a high-profile presenter is prepared to walk away</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1bcd20a4e33caf0e3352e3951d8f5d712eba90058f293a7eb754d21bc492432e</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T19:13:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261115-pragues-s-fight-for-public-tv-why-renowned-presenter-will-leave-czech-tv-over-reforms--1767661cd6ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261115-pragues-s-fight-for-public-tv-why-renowned-presenter-will-leave-czech-tv-over-reforms" /><summary type="html">Daniel Stach, one of the Czech Republic’s best-known television presenters and science journalists, tells Gavin Lee on France 24 why he is prepared to walk away from his career rather than work under changes he believes threaten the independence of public broadcasting.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Estonia to close Russian border crossings after 'sabotage' attempt at drone factory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:acf2482aa2b6a58af23926e580848e7f74162dfedb6b9c8b72591d186737c039</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T17:05:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261115-estonia-to-close-russian-border-crossings-after-sabotage-attempt-at-drone-factory--c99dd3720425.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261115-estonia-to-close-russian-border-crossings-after-sabotage-attempt-at-drone-factory" /><summary type="html">Estonia will close all its border crossing points with Russia from December 1, its ​foreign minister ‌said on Sunday, following a suspected ⁠sabotage attack on an Estonian defence company that Tallinn blamed on ‌Moscow. The Kremlin denied the accusations, calling them "entirely baseless".</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
